error_signature: "EGL_FOUND = FALSE|Error relocating .*libGLESv2|Error loading shared library libGLESv2\\.so|Error loading shared library libEGL\\.so|QOpenGLContext .* symbol not found|QSslConfiguration .* symbol not found|This plugin does not support createPlatformOpenGLContext"
root_cause: "OHOS device DOES ship a working GL stack — the gap is four mechanical layers, not a missing runtime: (1) the device exposes 'OpenHarmony EGL 1.4' as /system/lib64/libEGL.so + libGLESv3.so (GLES2 entry points live in libGLESv3; there is NO libGLESv2.so name); probe-verified eglInitialize/eglCreateContext/makeCurrent all OK, so no mesa/llvmpipe is needed; (2) Qt's FindEGL/FindGLESv2 are plain find_path/find_library that never search the OHOS SDK sysroot — enabling FEATURE_egl without explicit cache variables always dies with 'EGL_FOUND = FALSE'; (3) compiled GL libraries (libQt6Gui, libQt6Multimedia, ...) record NEEDED entries for libEGL.so/libGLESv2.so — if the conan package does not ship those two names, every GL consumer fails to load at runtime (Error relocating); (4) qtbase-sql-dbus-style split packages mirror the FULL qtbase library set and SHADOW the base qtbase in the merged farm and at runtime LD order — a split package still built with GL=OFF/SSL=OFF poisons the whole graph even after the base qtbase enables OpenGL (consumers load the old Gui/Network and die on QOpenGLContext/QSslConfiguration symbol not found). Separately, the offscreen QPA never implements createPlatformOpenGLContext, so GL verification must go through the wayland QPA behind a self-hosted compositor."
rec_approach: "qtbase recipe (6.11.1.4 verified): set INPUT_opengl=es2 + FEATURE_opengl/opengles2/egl=ON; derive the SDK sysroot from the profile compiler (tools.build:compiler_executables['c'] = .../ohos/native/llvm/bin/clang -> three dirs up -> native/, join 'sysroot'); inject EGL_INCLUDE_DIR=<sysroot>/usr/include, EGL_LIBRARY=<sysroot>/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-ohos/libEGL.so and GLESv2_INCLUDE_DIR/GLESv2_LIBRARY likewise as CMake cache variables; in package() ship libGLESv2.so and libEGL.so aliases by copying the sysroot stubs (fallback /system/lib64/libGLESv3.so and /system/lib64/libEGL.so) so consumer NEEDED entries resolve; SPLIT-PACKAGE DISCIPLINE: any qtbase-derived split package (qtbase-sql-dbus etc.) bumped in the same batch MUST port the same OpenGL AND openssl settings (resolve libssl/libcrypto via glob to tolerate libssl.so.3 layouts) or its mirrored stale Gui/Network shadows the fresh base libraries. Verification ladder, each rung independently observable: standalone EGL probe -> conan test_package with the same GL injection -> PyQt6 import matrix -> wayland self-hosted one-frame render (compositor setSocketName+create, not bare wl_display_add_socket — see DRAFT-ohos-wayland-gui-selfhosted-loop)."
match_keywords: ["EGL_FOUND", "libGLESv2", "libEGL", "QOpenGLContext symbol not found", "QSslConfiguration", "createPlatformOpenGLContext", "INPUT_opengl", "FEATURE_egl", "qtbase-sql-dbus", "sysroot", "OpenHarmony EGL"]
